From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephen Bates <sbates@raithlin.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Nov 2026 10:28:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ionic: free every temporary queue after a queue count change

ionic_reconfigure_queues() allocates the new rings in temporary qcqs,
swaps their contents with the live ones, and frees the temporaries,
which by then hold the old rings.  The loop that frees them runs up to
qparam->nxqs, but lif->nxqs and qparam->nxqs have been swapped just
above, so it runs up to the *old* queue count.

When the count grows into an index that has no qcq yet, a short
placeholder qcq is allocated so the swap has something to swap with,
and its rings and page pool end up in the temporary at that index --
which is beyond the old count, so it is never freed.  The qcq structs
themselves are devm allocations and go away at unbind, but the DMA
allocations do not, and the page pool stays listed with a pointer to a
NAPI that has been freed:

  ip link set $IF down; ethtool -L $IF combined 2; ip link set $IF up
  ethtool -L $IF combined 4; rmmod ionic

  DMA-API: pci 0000:01:00.0: device driver has pending DMA allocations
  while released from device [count=12]

and a later page pool dump over netlink reads the freed NAPI:

  BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in page_pool_nl_fill+0x690/0x730

Free the temporaries up to the larger of the two counts.  Both arrays
have room for every queue, and the loop already skips the entries that
were never allocated, so this frees exactly the ones that were missed.

Found while testing queue reconfiguration against the rocm-ernic
userspace emulated NIC, and reproduced with an unmodified driver.

The same bug is in mainline.  This is not upstream yet; it has been
reported to the AMD Pensando team, who have not replied.  Drop this
patch once the fix lands in the kernel IONIC_KERNEL_REF pins.

Fixes: 101b40a0171f ("ionic: change queue count with no reset")
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/pensando/ionic/ionic_lif.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/pensando/ionic/ionic_lif.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/pensando/ionic/ionic_lif.c
index abc8e3530435..15e878b6c13c 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/pensando/ionic/ionic_lif.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/pensando/ionic/ionic_lif.c
@@ -3144,8 +3144,11 @@ int ionic_reconfigure_queues(struct ionic_lif *lif,
 		err = ionic_start_queues_reconfig(lif);
 
 err_out:
-	/* free old allocs without cleaning intr */
-	for (i = 0; i < qparam->nxqs; i++) {
+	/* free old allocs without cleaning intr; the counts may have been
+	 * swapped above, and a placeholder's rings end up in the temporary
+	 * qcq of an index beyond the old count
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < max(qparam->nxqs, lif->nxqs); i++) {
 		if (tx_qcqs && tx_qcqs[i]) {
 			tx_qcqs[i]->flags &= ~IONIC_QCQ_F_INTR;
 			ionic_qcq_free(lif, tx_qcqs[i]);
-- 
